        <mxCell id="cap" value="This figure presents the Work Breakdown Structure of IDetect, an OCR-Based Discount ID Verification System, organized across four decomposition levels. At Level 1, IDetect serves as the single root of the system. At Level 2, it branches into five stakeholder-specific subsystems: the BPLO Portal, PDAO Portal, Client Portal (business establishment website and ID scanner), OSCA Portal, and Beneficiary App. At Level 3, each subsystem decomposes into its core functional modules, such as Establishment Provisioning, PWD Record Management, OCR Data Extraction, Real-time Verification, and Fraud Flag Investigation. At Level 4, these modules are further broken down into specific features including Camera Guidance &amp; Quality Check, Image Preprocessing, Confidence Scoring, Dual DB Query &amp; Status Return, Dispute Resolution, and Fraud Analytics &amp; Reporting, among others. This hierarchical structure reflects the modular and role-based design of IDetect, ensuring clear separation of responsibilities across government offices, business establishments, and beneficiaries within a unified verification and fraud management workflow." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1460" width="1300" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
